    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1619" root="ايم" body-key="A">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَيْمَ</span></b>  is a contraction of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَىُّ مَا</span>, meaning <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَىُّ شَىْءٍ</span>:
it is thus in the saying, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَيْمَ هُوَيَا فُلَانُ</span> [<i>What
thing is it, O such a one?</i>]: and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَيْمَ تَقُولُ</span> [<i>What
thing sayest thou?</i>]. (TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اَيْمُ ٱللّٰهِ</span> [for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اَيْمُنُ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ٱللّٰهِ</span>]: see in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يمن</span>. (K.)

